                <pb facs="0193" n="79" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg79"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.51/2254: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Herod</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-01-09T14:00:00-04:40"><hi rendition="#italic">January 9,
                                1922—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 10—9:45
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>3. Your 1, January 7, 2 p.m. My action was to give [Military Governor] as
                    instructed your 27, December 21, 1 p.m. I gave Military Governor copy of
                    paraphrase of same made for Legation files. Your instructions number 429,
                    December 23rd has not been received yet. The Dominican Government is still
                    unable to sell the certificates here.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Herod</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
